FIX DEPLOYED 2026-10-09 (day 8): Lane b830k merged (3b50c7ce) — ROOT CAUSE: Lwt.choose in start_background_task_loop abandons the losing enqueue-condition waiter every 5s tick; ~49 words/waiter x 720/h = +35K words/h, present since B712 (June 27). Fix: Lwt.pick (cancels loser) as wait_for_enqueue_or_tick + lifetime regression suite (300-waiter retention check). In-vitro: 49.00 words/tick before -> 0.00 after. CORRECTION to earlier note: heap-scan 'prompt families' were sqlite page cache + list_tasks 5s churn (loads ALL task prompts per tick — PERF follow-up candidate, not retention); true retained blocks were waiter promise/closures. Daemon restarted pid 3087597 on fix. VERIFICATION PENDING: hourly gc_live_words floor should flatten within 24h (previously +36K/h). x-p35 suite debt now spans 10f831ac..3b50c7ce (VPN still down). Per-loop policy this deploy restart is diagnostic, no clock reset; the clock itself (from Oct 7) now tracks a FIXED-and-verifying daemon.

